title: Palo Alto Networks: Public IP address usage
agents: paloalto_api
catalog: hw/network/paloalto
license: GPLv2
distribution: checkmk-paloalto-api
description:
 Counts how many addresses of an allocated public block are in use, so that a
 block running out is noticed before it does. An address counts as used when
 it appears in a NAT rule (every vsys rulebase plus the shared one, read
 through a scoped xpath), in the ARP table, or on a logical interface. The
 same address is counted once no matter how often it occurs.

 By default the usable size of the block is the denominator, that is the size
 minus its network and broadcast address. If the block is routed to the
 firewall rather than on-link, every address can be handed out; set "Count the
 network and broadcast address as usable" in the rule "Palo Alto public IP
 addresses" for that. Default levels are 80/90 percent; lower levels on the
 number of free addresses can be set instead, which is usually the more
 natural way to think about a small block.

 Only blocks the firewall itself can see are counted. Addresses that live on
 another device, a border router for example, do not appear in any of the
 three sources and would be reported as unused.

item:
 The network in CIDR notation, e.g. "203.0.113.0/24".

discovery:
 One service per network configured in the special agent rule.
